Compute the degeneracy \(\delta(G)\) of \(G\);
Compute-DC\((G,1,\delta(G))\);
ConstructHierarchy\((G,sc(\cdot,\cdot))\); /* See Algorithm 4 */;
return \(\mathcal{T}\);

Procedure Compute-DC\((g,L,H)\)
if \(L = H\) then
    for each edge \((u,v) \in E(g)\) do \(sc(u,v) \leftarrow L\);
else
    Choose an integer \(M\) such that \(L < M \leq H\);
    \(\phi_M(g) \leftarrow KECC(g,M)\); /* Compute \(M\)-ECCs of \(g\) */;
    Let \(g_1\) be the graph obtained from \(g\) by contracting each connected subgraph of \(\phi_M(g)\) into a super-vertex, and \(g_2\) be \(\phi_M(g)\); /* \(g_1 = \mathrm{GS}_L^{M-1}(G)\), \(g_2 = \mathrm{GS}_M^H(G)\) */;
    Compute-DC\((g_1,L,M-1)\);
    Compute-DC\((g_2,M,H)\);
